  "semanticKeywords": "•\tRegisters a query_risk_exposure tool that combines load history and weather outlooks with market data — forward strips, capacity tags, and locational pricing — to project exposure rather than report history.\n•\tQuantifies each exposure in dollars and shows the assumptions behind it, for example “4CP exposure for summer is moderate-to-elevated, roughly $184K in capacity charges, peak risk window late July to early August.”\n•\tPresents mitigation tradeoffs, for example hedging a portion of an open position now versus deferring, without recommending one; the user makes the call.\n•\tCites the market data, forecast window, and methodology behind every projection, so the reasoning — not just the number — is auditable.\n•\tOperates under the strictest Guardrail of the three: every output is framed as advisory decision support, and the agent does not issue directives on financial positions.",
  "semanticUseCases": "The Risk Agent is the forecasting lane: it projects a portfolio's forward financial exposure to energy markets and presents the tradeoffs of mitigating it. Where the Energy Agent reports what a building used and the Facilities Agent explains current behavior, the Risk Agent looks ahead — quantifying coincident-peak (4CP) risk, capacity charge exposure, and price volatility on open positions in dollar terms. It is advisory by design: it frames the levers and their tradeoffs as decision support and stops short of directing a specific action.",
  "agenticWorkflowId": "f1c5d831-b832-4105-8225-720eca07298e",
  "enableForAutoInvoke": false,
  "semanticSearchEnabled": true,
  "isAvailableForMigration": false
